00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.310 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  modern agriculture today faces two big  challenges an increased demand for food  and growing more sustainably  the farm to fork strategy at the heart  of the european green deal is helping  with this second objective  more sustainable farming will also make  the food we eat healthier  one of the eu's key farm default  commitments is to reduce by 2030 the  overall use and risk of chemical  pesticides by 50 percent  promoting safer alternatives to  pesticides is a top priority at the  agricultural college  here agricultural experts apply  protocols created by the defease network  a french public initiative that helps  farmers deal with more sustainable  methods of production  some of their actions include tailored  crop strategies ways to avoid products  that pollute and reinforcing plant  immunity with natural biostimulants  a coordinated strategy like this has  direct advantages for the environment  and farmer's health it can also have a  positive impact on economic returns  we have a national database which has  shown that the reduction of pesticides  has no impact on the operating margin  as we use less pesticides we might  expect a smaller yield but there are  less costs in the end the margin is  almost the same  mechanical weeding plays an important  role in soil management this technique  used in specific conditions helps  farmers remove partial amounts of the  herbicides widely used in crop  production  thanks to this method we could reduce  the use of herbicides further to do so  you have to use this machine at the  right time in the right way and with the  right setting so as to not compromise  the development of the crop  within the framework of national and eu  initiatives education also plays an  important role  the students of the agricultural college  represent the next generation of farmers  those who will deal with a more  sustainable way to produce food with new  rules  for them a cultural transformation is  underway even in the rural world  i've got the impression that things are  accelerating before we were much more  focused on pesticides now a lot of  farmers are changing my father is an  organic farmer i know we can grow  produce in a different way  nowadays we should use other methods to  be able to get the same yield  to have a better quality of food  and to preserve our environment our  planet  [Music]  the farm run by the campus carries out  its own crop cultivation and breeding  activities its ultimate goal is to turn  the entire production organic but until  then the current approach is already  improving the quality of the soil and of  the food chain  biology starts in the soil if there's  life in the soil we give life to the  plants and the animals if the plant is  healthy at the beginning the animal will  eat this plant and will produce healthy  milk and meat automatically we consume  this milk and meat and we have healthy  food  [Music]

